# PROJECT BRIEF: IISER MOHALI COMPUTER CENTRE — STAFF DIRECTORY & DUTY MANAGEMENT PORTAL

## 1. Project Overview

Design and develop a fully functional, secure, responsive, and professionally designed website for the **Computer Centre, Indian Institute of Science Education and Research (IISER) Mohali**.

The website will serve as an internal administrative portal for the IISER Mohali community.

Its central purpose is to maintain a comprehensive database of the Computer Centre team, including the Head of the Computer Centre and all staff members, their responsibilities, assigned duties, working schedules, and contact information.

An authenticated user should be able to visit the website, search for a particular technical or administrative task, and immediately identify the staff member responsible for it on a particular day.

The website must have two distinct levels of access:

1. **Administrator (Head of Computer Centre):** Complete authority to add, remove, edit, and manage staff members and their assigned duties.
2. **Regular IISER Community Member:** Read-only access to the staff directory, responsibilities, schedules, and duty assignments.

This must be a real, functional web application, not merely a static website or UI prototype.

