### Important implementation instruction

Work systematically.

First establish the project architecture and authentication feasibility. Then implement the database and backend permissions, followed by the frontend.

Do not build a visually complete but functionally fake application.

If institutional authentication credentials, API documentation, SSO metadata, server access, or administrator details are unavailable, explicitly identify what is missing. Do not fabricate an integration or claim that institutional authentication works when it has not been tested.

The final objective is to deliver a production-quality internal Computer Centre portal that IISER Mohali can actually adopt, maintain, and use.

**Design philosophy:** An elegant, recognisably IISER Mohali institutional experience, backed by a secure and reliable administrative system.

**Core principle:** Any member of the IISER community should be able to find the right Computer Centre staff member for a particular task in a matter of seconds.